# Accessibility audit: Empty (2026-11-15)

Scope: `spec/components/empty/contract.json`, `src/components/empty/*` (`sb-empty`, `sb-empty-header`, `sb-empty-media`, `sb-empty-title`, `sb-empty-description`, `sb-empty-content`), `playwright/tests/empty/*`. Standard: WCAG 2.2 AA; static layout container with no role (no APG pattern).

## Criteria

| POUR | Criterion | Result | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| P | 1.4.3 text contrast | Pass | Contract pairs (description fg on background, icon fg on icon bg, link hover fg on background) pass in light and dark; `npm run check` T6 passes |
| P | 1.4.11 non-text contrast | Not applicable | Icon box is decorative (svg `aria-hidden`); no border or control identified by color; the optional dashed border is consumer-owned |
| P | 1.4.1 color alone | Pass | Description links are underlined (probe: `text-decoration-line: underline`); hover only changes color on top of the underline |
| P | 1.4.10 reflow | Pass | Probe at 320px wide: `scrollWidth` 320, no horizontal scroll; content max 48ch with `min-width: 0` |
| P | forced-colors | Pass | Probe with `forced-colors: active`: svg stroke and description text compute to `rgb(0, 0, 0)` (CanvasText) on Canvas white; the muted icon box background is dropped by the UA, which is harmless because the icon is decorative and still visible |
| P | prefers-reduced-motion | Not applicable | No transitions or animation in `Empty.scss` |
| P | 1.3.1 info and relationships | Pass | Title is deliberately a visual label; the contract tells authors to place a real heading inside `sb-empty-title` when it belongs in the outline. Nothing is conveyed by structure the component hides |
| O | 2.1.1 / 2.1.2 keyboard, trap | Pass | No focusable part of its own; slotted `sb-button` and `a` keep native Tab order (probe: Tab lands on the description link); no trap |
| O | 2.4.7 focus visible | Pass | Slotted link shows the UA focus ring (probe: `outline-style: auto`, 1px, `rgb(0, 95, 204)`); buttons are owned by `sb-button` |
| O | 2.5.8 target size | Pass (exception) | Description link is 17px high but is an inline link inside a sentence (WCAG 2.5.8 inline exception); buttons are owned by `sb-button` |
| U | 3.2.x predictable, 3.3.x errors, labels | Not applicable | No input, no name by design (contract `accessibleNameSource`: none) |
| R | 4.1.2 role, name, state | Pass | CDP `Accessibility.getFullAXTree` on all 4 stories: all six elements are `generic` (no role added), text is exposed as static text, `sb-button` exposes `button` with its name, the description link exposes `link: Clear filters`, the decorative svg is absent |
| R | ID references across shadow roots | Not applicable | No ID references; no ARIA on any element |
| R | No roles or ARIA | Pass | Behavior spec asserts no `role` or `aria-*` attribute on any element of the family |
| R | axe | Pass | Behavior spec: axe clean on default, outline, default-media and title-only |
| R | Behavior spec and `npm run check` | Pass | 11/11 passed (the first run had one navigation timeout on the axe test while the dev server was warming up; the rerun passed 11/11); all checks pass (A1 warn on spec/api.json is unrelated) |
| R | Screen-reader evidence | Pass | AX tree above plus the `__screen-reader__` snapshots (check S1) |

## Failures

None.

## Verdict
Verdict: ready
Approved-by: Davecelot (2026-11-15)

Static container with correct (absent) semantics: no role or ARIA, decorative media hidden from the accessibility tree, links underlined with a visible focus ring, reflow and forced colors hold, axe and the behavior spec (11/11) and `npm run check` pass. No open findings.
